{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>קנה</b> Three times in the Masorah: לא כי קנה (Samuel 24:24), אקנה בכסף מלא, כי קנו. אקנה מאותך במחיר — when he purchased the threshing floor from Aravnah. For even though we derive או קנה מיד עמיתך — that you should purchase from the hand of an Israelite and not from the hand of a gentile — even so, David purchased the threshing floor from Aravnah, since he could not purchase from an Israelite." "<b>א</b> ל תונו איש את אחיו. And adjacent to it: במספר לו — a thing that is by measure or by weight has no אונאה."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The three cited phrases appear to be the three occurrences of קנה in the Masorah; the third phrase כי קנו could not be identified with certainty."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:20:33.401408251Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}